        must="Solve multi-step real-world problems with the order of operations, exponents and radicals, in six steps or fewer, and report the answer with its unit.",
        must_not="No keyword strategy and no CUBES — the state guide names circling numbers and boxing key words as a misconception, not a method. No PEMDAS.",

        read_first=[
            "This is Math Nation 4.7 and 4.8 in one period, merged under ruling 30. Lesson 8 is three rotating stations in the book; under ruling 10 it is taught from the front, and its mathematics survives as the cost items here.",
            "The guide's fourth named misconception for this benchmark is keyword hunting — 'circling the numbers, underlining the question, boxing in key words, and eliminating important contextual information'. Notes II attacks it directly with two problems built from the same three numbers and the same two words whose answers are 39 and 66, and whiteboard 9 asks for the contrast in writing. Do not teach a keyword strategy anywhere in this lesson, and do not leave one on the wall.",
            "One book defect is repaired rather than reproduced, and it is the worst structural one in the unit. Math Nation's flooring item — Dominic in Practice and Homework 4.8, Liliana in the Teacher Edition — puts underlay under the Bathroom heading in its table while its price sits inside the bedroom's area group in the expression, and prices grout per square foot in the table while adding it as a flat amount in the expression. As printed, 'the cost of carpeting the bedroom', 'bedroom only' and 'bathroom only' have no unambiguous answer. Example 2, boards 4 and 6 and bank 5, 6, 11 rebuild the context with the question saying which prices are rates and which are flat.",
            "Also not reproduced: TE 4.8.2 question 1b, which asks for the part of the expression that represents the cost of CARPETING the bedroom and circles carpet plus padding plus underlay — 375.84 dollars where carpeting alone is 234.09.",
            "Whiteboard 7 is the state guide's backyard task reduced to its arithmetic, and it is the one item in this lesson tagged out of the radicand scan: 200 is not a perfect square, the root is carried exactly, and the rounding happens once at the end. A board that answers 84 rounded the side to 14 first — name that rather than mark it, because it is the point of the board."],
        standard_notes=[("Clarification", "Multi-step expressions are limited to six steps or fewer. Instruction avoids mnemonics such as PEMDAS and keyword strategies such as CUBES."),
                        ("Boundary", "Radicands stay inside the benchmark's lists except where a real measurement produces one that does not, in which case the root is carried exactly and rounded once at the end.")],
        sits="The last two book lessons of MA.8.NSO.1.7, taught as one period, and the last teaching day of Unit 4. The unit assessment follows the review; every 8.NSO.1.7 item on it is a given expression, so the formulas here are the bridge between the benchmark and the way the test asks it.",
        lives="Notes II — 'read what is happening, not which words are there'. Board 6 is the diagnostic on cost structure and board 9 asks for the whole idea in writing, with two answers and a reason.",
        materials="Whiteboards and markers. Calculators are allowed on everything and are the right tool for the BMI and kinetic-energy items; the work being assessed is the expression, not the arithmetic.",
        variation="Questions 1–4 substitute into four shapes: a coefficient with a power, a formula with two letters, a fraction bar, and a binomial inside a power. 5 and 6 are cost expressions — one square, one rectangle — where the student has to decide what multiplies the area. 7 and 8 are two real formulas, each evaluated three times, so the structure is fixed and only the numbers move; 7 also requires rounding to a stated place. 9 works backwards in three shapes, ending with a cost equation that has to be unwound. The pattern breaks at 10, where two problems with the same numbers and the same words have different answers. 11 is the diagnostic multiple choice on cost structure and 12 the select-all on what an exponent is attached to. The Additional sheet mirrors each position.",
        audit=["Every item re-derived by sympy at build time (mathcheck: 0 findings). Every radicand and exponent gap scanned (capcheck: 0 findings outside the two tagged blocks, Notes III and whiteboard 7, where a real measurement gives a non-perfect radicand).",
               "The body-mass-index formula is the standard imperial one, B = 703w/h² for w in pounds and h in inches, and every value is carried exactly and rounded once: 24.958 → 25.0, 25.824 → 25.8, 27.122 → 27.1.",
               "Kinetic energy is K = ½mv² with m in kilograms and v in metres per second, giving joules; 1,200 kg at 15 m/s is 135,000 J.",
               "Math Nation 4.7 and 4.8 values verified in the audit: 4.7.2 Rodney (28,394 in³), 4.7.4 (2/5, 50.25, 2,976 J), 4.8.1 (−151/4 and 0), 4.8.2 Liliana (455.47 and 375.84), 4.8.3 Phillip (706.56 and 2,156.25), 4.8.4 Michaela (8,886), and all ten items of both Practice 4.7 and Homework 4.7. The flooring ambiguity and the 4.8.2 key are the two defects, both listed above.",
               "The guide's backyard task verified: a side of √200 ≈ 14.1421 feet, six sides giving 84.8528 → 84.85 feet, and the 6-foot panels at 10.0083 dollars a foot beating the 8-foot panels at 11.0825."],
        changes=["4.7.1 Warm-Up (a Mark Cuban quotation and an acronym exercise, with no mathematics in it) → spaced retrieval under ruling 31.",
                 "4.7.2 Collaboration (Rodney) → Notes I and Example 1, taught from the front.",
                 "4.7.3 and 4.7.4 → Example 1's Your Turn, the independent set and the banks; the margin note telling teachers students have no calculator on 'the FSA' is not reproduced, and the test is the FAST.",
                 "4.8's three rotating stations (Liliana, Phillip, Michaela) → Example 2, boards 4 and 6 and the banks, taught from the front, with the flooring table's ambiguity removed.",
                 "4.7.5 and 4.8.5 Wrap-Up reflections → the period ends with the independent set and IXL under rulings 10 and 21; whiteboard 9 is the exit evidence."],
